{
  "meta": {
    "schema_version": "3.0",
    "supersedes": "keyword_lexicon.json @ 2.0",
    "status": "live",
    "description": "Keyword cluster catalog, schema 3.0. Each cluster declares parent_theme + parent_subtheme as FKs into codebook.next.json. Variants are SUGGESTION FUEL ONLY — they rank cluster suggestions in the segment tag drawer; they do NOT auto-tag any occurrence. Per-instance tag rows continue to live in keyword_tags.json, keyed by (cluster_id, segment_id, char_start, char_end).",
    "changelog": [
      "3.0-draft — replaced the `categories[].keywords[]` shape with a flat `clusters[]` keyed by parent_theme + parent_subtheme. The 102 clusters from keyword_lexicon.json @ 2.0 will be re-classified via the codebook-migration map in codebook_migration_map.json; some will split into parallel clusters with different parents (e.g. cost as a treatment vs. trial barrier).",
      "3.0-draft (porting pass) — ported 103 clusters from keyword_lexicon.json @ 2.0 via scripts/migrate-keyword-lexicon.mjs. Each cluster carries parent_theme + parent_subtheme assigned by category default + per-cluster overrides. Descriptions are empty for now; analyst should backfill as part of Phase 0 review."
    ],
    "cluster_shape": {
      "id": "Slug, lowercase + underscores. Globally unique. Example: 'treatment_cost_concerns'.",
      "label": "Display label. Example: 'Treatment cost concerns'.",
      "description": "One sentence describing what the cluster covers.",
      "parent_theme": "FK → codebook.next.json themes[].id. Required.",
      "parent_subtheme": "FK → codebook.next.json themes[].subthemes[].id. Required. The named subtheme must belong to the named parent_theme.",
      "variants": "Array of lowercase surface forms (spellings, plurals, brand/generic pairs, multi-word phrasings) used to RANK this cluster's suggestion priority when an analyst highlights a phrase in the drawer. Matching is case-insensitive, with hyphen/space runs treated as equivalent. Not used for auto-tagging."
    },
    "matching_notes": [
      "Matching for suggestions is case-insensitive. Within a variant, runs of spaces/hyphens match any run of whitespace or hyphens (so 'out of pocket' also matches 'out-of-pocket').",
      "Variants with no separator (e.g. 'glp1') are listed explicitly because the separator in multi-word variants is required, not optional.",
      "Brand and generic names for the same molecule should be grouped under one cluster (e.g. semaglutide groups Wegovy/Ozempic).",
      "Suggestion ranking may additionally weight clusters by the segment's current theme/subtheme tags — clusters whose parent_subtheme matches a tagged subtheme float to the top.",
      "If the same surface concept needs to belong under different parent subthemes (e.g. cost as a Treatment Barrier vs. as a Trial Barrier), create two clusters with parallel names and different parent_subtheme values — do NOT add a cluster to multiple parents."
    ],
    "example_cluster": {
      "id": "treatment_cost_concerns",
      "label": "Treatment cost concerns",
      "description": "Out-of-pocket cost, insurance friction, and affordability as obstacles to starting or continuing treatment.",
      "parent_theme": "treatment",
      "parent_subtheme": "treatment_barriers",
      "variants": [
        "cost",
        "costs",
        "expensive",
        "afford",
        "affordable",
        "out of pocket",
        "out-of-pocket",
        "price",
        "prohibitive"
      ]
    }
  },
